MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The adjustable power supply and 220-ohm resistors feel like useful next purchases because they help me power and test circuits with my breadboards and existing components.",
    "Simple indicator LEDs and magnet wire connect meaningfully to my earlier LED kit and ferrite cores, even though I do not need more LEDs or a full spool of wire today."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Brass stock and the AC motor controller require projects I have not shown a need for; working with small electronic components does not mean I am machining parts or controlling mains-powered motors.",
    "Automatically flashing LEDs, specialized measurement leads, and solder paste do not fit my immediate tasks: I prefer controllable indicators, have no identified instrument for those leads, and can use my breadboards without solder paste."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The recommendations seem to treat electronics and workshop supplies as broadly interchangeable, while the specific job each item supports matters much more to me.",
    "Having bought a component seems to be taken as a reason to buy more related supplies immediately, even when I already have enough or need a specific project first."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "I am more likely to choose something that makes my existing breadboard components usable together than something that introduces a separate kind of project.",
    "Relevance alone is not enough for me to buy: another bulk LED pack duplicates supplies I have, magnet wire can wait for a winding project, and choosing one power supply removes my immediate need for the other."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my interest in small circuit projects but sometimes confuse related equipment with something I can use and need right now."
}
